WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.206 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:24.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:27.374 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:28.379 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of that day.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.936 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:30.936 --> 00:00:32.698 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:35.798 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:36.796 --> 00:00:39.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

00:00:39.824 --> 00:00:41.958 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A range is the top and the bottom,

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:44.339 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two lines,

00:00:44.339 --> 00:00:46.637 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:47.157 --> 00:00:49.195 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:49.195 --> 00:00:51.088 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the range.

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:53.507 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:53.507 --> 00:00:55.407 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:56.331 --> 00:00:57.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in

00:00:57.839 --> 00:00:59.778 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:03.269 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:04.276 --> 00:01:06.121 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:06.121 --> 00:01:07.853 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:11.786 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook, the three

00:01:11.786 --> 00:01:14.269 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words from lesson one, range, levels

00:01:14.269 --> 00:01:16.495 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and stop, the pair, paper or a demo

00:01:16.495 --> 00:01:18.892 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
account, no secrets, a written stop,

00:01:18.892 --> 00:01:21.461 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the word Example on every figure.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.361 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:25.222 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:25.222 --> 00:01:26.339 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:26.592 --> 00:01:27.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you

00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:29.553 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawing a grid with no edges.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.207 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you

00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:32.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and what you pay with.

00:01:33.034 --> 00:01:34.498 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:34.498 --> 00:01:36.032 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:36.552 --> 00:01:38.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:40.956 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:41.248 --> 00:01:43.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:43.447 --> 00:01:44.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair is

00:01:44.955 --> 00:01:46.594 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:47.114 --> 00:01:49.306 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:49.826 --> 00:01:51.245 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:01:51.245 --> 00:01:52.195 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of the day.

00:01:52.688 --> 00:01:54.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.248 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:58.653 --> 00:02:01.238 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:01.758 --> 00:02:03.782 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:03.782 --> 00:02:05.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.618 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:08.618 --> 00:02:10.685 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

00:02:10.685 --> 00:02:12.864 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:13.298 --> 00:02:15.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

00:02:15.646 --> 00:02:18.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a daily close finishes outside the range

00:02:18.141 --> 00:02:20.635 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:02:21.155 --> 00:02:22.976 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.645 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:25.165 --> 00:02:27.176 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the three

00:02:27.176 --> 00:02:29.075 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:29.945 --> 00:02:32.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.284 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:34.284 --> 00:02:35.691 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:36.211 --> 00:02:37.608 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:37.608 --> 00:02:39.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:39.594 --> 00:02:41.937 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:41.937 --> 00:02:44.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account,

00:02:44.279 --> 00:02:46.465 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and sometimes move money out of it.

00:02:46.985 --> 00:02:49.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:49.612 --> 00:02:51.985 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:54.824 --> 00:02:56.779 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:57.254 --> 00:02:58.885 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:02:58.885 --> 00:03:00.671 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:01.721 --> 00:03:03.694 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the range onto the page,

00:03:03.694 --> 00:03:05.137 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not every day's prices.

00:03:05.657 --> 00:03:07.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:07.891 --> 00:03:10.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:12.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:03:12.011 --> 00:03:13.352 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the range.

00:03:13.775 --> 00:03:15.178 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:17.844 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, range,

00:03:17.844 --> 00:03:19.299 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:22.033 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with no

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.404 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:03:26.404 --> 00:03:28.576 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the range

00:03:28.576 --> 00:03:30.670 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.453 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:33.503 --> 00:03:35.515 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:37.971 --> 00:03:39.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.961 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:42.391 --> 00:03:43.914 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:43.914 --> 00:03:45.209 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:45.729 --> 00:03:47.126 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.651 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:50.562 --> 00:03:52.629 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:54.822 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:55.206 --> 00:03:56.684 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:56.684 --> 00:03:58.093 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.736 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:01.861 --> 00:04:03.034 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:03.437 --> 00:04:04.834 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.066 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:07.401 --> 00:04:10.592 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the July

00:04:10.592 --> 00:04:13.683 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window, the public

00:04:13.683 --> 00:04:16.376 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

00:04:16.376 --> 00:04:18.969 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October 2023, so you buy the base,

00:04:18.969 --> 00:04:21.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.454 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:24.974 --> 00:04:26.985 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:27.207 --> 00:04:28.788 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We price in US dollars.

00:04:29.308 --> 00:04:31.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your exchange may charge fees

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.532 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars, so

00:04:32.532 --> 00:04:34.097 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
keep each in its own column.

00:04:34.594 --> 00:04:36.770 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.946 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:38.946 --> 00:04:41.028 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:41.548 --> 00:04:43.454 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and

00:04:43.454 --> 00:04:45.970 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.605 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:50.361 --> 00:04:54.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the July to October example window

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:58.526 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:04:59.046 --> 00:05:00.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:05:00.946 --> 00:05:02.845 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.294 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:05:05.294 --> 00:05:07.293 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:05:07.813 --> 00:05:09.669 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:05:09.669 --> 00:05:11.680 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:05:12.113 --> 00:05:14.003 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you

00:05:14.003 --> 00:05:15.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
got it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:15.971 --> 00:05:17.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:18.911 --> 00:05:20.182 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has

00:05:20.182 --> 00:05:21.523 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to say what you will do.

00:05:21.973 --> 00:05:23.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.190 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.832 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the range,

00:05:28.832 --> 00:05:30.588 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom,

00:05:30.588 --> 00:05:32.711 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the second close still outside.

00:05:33.231 --> 00:05:34.795 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:34.795 --> 00:05:36.383 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders,

00:05:36.383 --> 00:05:38.282 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:38.794 --> 00:05:40.582 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:41.544 --> 00:05:44.274 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:44.274 --> 00:05:46.771 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:47.291 --> 00:05:49.307 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:49.307 --> 00:05:51.107 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:51.627 --> 00:05:53.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:55.861 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and

00:05:55.861 --> 00:05:58.090 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the exchange runs it, not this course.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.614 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:06:00.614 --> 00:06:02.469 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:06:02.989 --> 00:06:05.056 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:06:05.056 --> 00:06:06.620 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.423 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services

00:06:09.423 --> 00:06:12.042 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:12.042 --> 00:06:14.661 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:14.661 --> 00:06:16.973 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:17.493 --> 00:06:18.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:18.757 --> 00:06:20.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:20.609 --> 00:06:22.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:25.977 --> 00:06:28.212 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:28.491 --> 00:06:31.087 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:31.607 --> 00:06:33.489 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:33.489 --> 00:06:34.719 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:35.239 --> 00:06:37.710 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, new licensing rules

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.345 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for platforms that hold crypto for you

00:06:40.345 --> 00:06:42.486 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
are phased in through that year.

00:06:43.006 --> 00:06:45.017 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:45.145 --> 00:06:47.125 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:47.125 --> 00:06:48.578 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your

00:06:51.285 --> 00:06:53.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password, is two-factor authentication.

00:06:54.244 --> 00:06:56.344 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:06:56.864 --> 00:06:58.897 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:06:59.483 --> 00:07:01.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:07:01.525 --> 00:07:03.145 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:07:04.195 --> 00:07:05.704 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is when your waiting

00:07:05.704 --> 00:07:06.991 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order actually trades.

00:07:07.511 --> 00:07:09.801 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:11.924 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:12.134 --> 00:07:13.810 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.542 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:15.878 --> 00:07:17.577 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:17.577 --> 00:07:19.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:19.795 --> 00:07:21.248 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:21.248 --> 00:07:22.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:25.932 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:26.452 --> 00:07:29.531 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:29.531 --> 00:07:32.292 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:32.812 --> 00:07:34.935 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:35.257 --> 00:07:37.101 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:37.101 --> 00:07:39.032 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:39.552 --> 00:07:41.590 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.173 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the July

00:07:43.173 --> 00:07:44.843 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window.

00:07:45.363 --> 00:07:47.674 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:47.674 --> 00:07:50.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:07:50.151 --> 00:07:52.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:07:53.312 --> 00:07:54.857 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:07:54.857 --> 00:07:56.180 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.286 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin built

00:08:01.286 --> 00:08:03.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay worth about one US dollar.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.640 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:08:06.109 --> 00:08:08.287 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A swap is trading one coin for another.

00:08:08.743 --> 00:08:10.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price is in a stablecoin,

00:08:10.731 --> 00:08:12.003 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill is a swap.

00:08:13.053 --> 00:08:15.258 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated record

00:08:15.258 --> 00:08:16.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of every bot: the plan,

00:08:16.551 --> 00:08:18.452 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the changes, the fills, the fees,

00:08:18.452 --> 00:08:20.353 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a review note of what happened,

00:08:20.353 --> 00:08:22.558 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and whether you followed the rules.

00:08:23.078 --> 00:08:24.866 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:25.215 --> 00:08:27.349 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:27.869 --> 00:08:30.181 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

00:08:30.181 --> 00:08:32.132 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every swap goes in the journal.

00:08:32.652 --> 00:08:34.937 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is also the page you will

00:08:34.937 --> 00:08:37.146 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:08:37.666 --> 00:08:40.191 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:08:40.191 --> 00:08:42.243 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

00:08:42.243 --> 00:08:44.690 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the value

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars at the time,

00:08:46.899 --> 00:08:49.346 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

00:08:49.346 --> 00:08:51.635 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it was for, and who the other side was.

00:08:52.155 --> 00:08:54.229 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:08:54.229 --> 00:08:55.996 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, the gaps, the money

00:08:55.996 --> 00:08:57.455 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in the bot, the stop rule,

00:08:57.455 --> 00:08:59.606 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fills, the fees, the Australian

00:08:59.606 --> 00:09:01.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar value of each fill, a review

00:09:01.757 --> 00:09:03.768 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:09:04.274 --> 00:09:05.911 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The Australian dollar value

00:09:05.911 --> 00:09:07.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column is the one exception.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.509 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is for your tax records.

00:09:10.026 --> 00:09:12.129 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:09:12.129 --> 00:09:14.140 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:09:14.561 --> 00:09:15.567 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records

00:09:15.567 --> 00:09:16.908 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for at least five years.

00:09:17.264 --> 00:09:19.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:09:19.036 --> 00:09:19.922 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:09:20.442 --> 00:09:22.230 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:22.649 --> 00:09:23.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:24.332 --> 00:09:26.623 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:26.757 --> 00:09:27.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:28.379 --> 00:09:30.223 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:30.883 --> 00:09:33.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask

00:09:33.133 --> 00:09:34.966 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for a seed phrase, a private

00:09:34.966 --> 00:09:36.300 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.795 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:09:38.795 --> 00:09:40.218 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, or asks for one

00:09:40.218 --> 00:09:41.878 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of those, treat it as a scam.

00:09:42.398 --> 00:09:43.627 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:09:44.639 --> 00:09:47.091 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:09:47.091 --> 00:09:49.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:09:49.775 --> 00:09:50.780 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:09:51.771 --> 00:09:53.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now cover the chart and say your

00:09:53.767 --> 00:09:55.763 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
page out loud: the pair, the range,

00:09:55.763 --> 00:09:57.376 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the stop rule.

00:09:57.896 --> 00:09:59.897 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

00:09:59.897 --> 00:10:01.590 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.230 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:06.350 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase,

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.896 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a private key, or an API secret.

00:10:11.416 --> 00:10:13.092 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:10:13.491 --> 00:10:15.169 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own

00:10:15.169 --> 00:10:17.056 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
notebook so a practice sketch is

00:10:17.056 --> 00:10:19.154 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
never later mistaken for a live plan.

00:10:20.204 --> 00:10:22.583 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:10:22.583 --> 00:10:24.725 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:24.725 --> 00:10:27.025 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:28.225 --> 00:10:30.208 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What is a grid bot.

00:10:30.728 --> 00:10:32.348 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your range,

00:10:32.348 --> 00:10:33.968 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.567 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:36.857 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:10:37.377 --> 00:10:39.025 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:10:39.025 --> 00:10:40.645 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

